hadiths[400]{hadithnumber,text}:
"609","""Do you know why it is named Ramadan? It is because it burns away sins."""
"610","""Do not say 'Ramadan' because it is the name of Allah; rather, you should say 'the month of Ramadan.'"""
"611","""Fast and you will become healthy."""
"612","""Everything has its zakat, and the zakat of the body is fasting."""
"613","""Every hair of the fasting person glorifies Allah for him, and on the Day of Resurrection, a golden tablecloth will be spread under the Throne for fasting men and fasting women."""
"614","""If Allah Almighty were to grant permission to the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth to speak, they would give glad tidings of Paradise to those who fast in the month of Ramadan."""
"615","""Whoever misses one fast of Ramadan without a valid excuse, upon him are fasts of one month."""
"616","""Whoever misses one fast of Ramadan should offer the sacrifice of a camel."""
"617","""Whoever missed one fast of Ramadan and died before making it up, then for each day, it is obligatory to feed one needy person with one mudd (approximately half a kilogram) of food."""
"618","""Whoever breaks his fast with a date earned through lawful means, four hundred prayers are added to his prayers."""
"619","""When Ramadan is sound, the whole year is sound."""
"620","""Every day of Ramadan, Allah Almighty frees six hundred thousand people from Hell."""
"621","""Allah Almighty frees one million people from Hell at the time of Iftar every night in Ramadan."""
"622","""The supplication of a fasting person at the time of breaking the fast is not rejected."""
"623","""Three people will not be questioned (on the Day of Resurrection) about food and drink: ① The one who breaks his fast ② The one who eats the pre-dawn meal (suhoor) ③ The one who hosts a guest."""
"624","""Three things do not break the fast: ① Vomiting ② Cupping ③ Wet dream"""
"625","""Whoever looked at a woman in such a way that, even behind her clothes, the size of her bones became apparent to him, and he was fasting, then his fast is broken."""
"626","""A person who fasts during Ramadan while traveling is like one who does not fast while residing (i.e., in a state of residence)."""
"627","""Whoever dies while he still owes fasts, then for each day, a poor person should be fed on his behalf."""
"628","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on the Day of Arafah in the plain of Arafat."""
"629","""Fast on the day of Ashura (the 10th of Muharram), and in opposition to the Jews, also fast one day before it or one day after it."""
"630","""Mamoola is the first bird that observed the fast of Ashura."""
"631","""Whoever is generous towards his family on the day of Ashura, Allah Almighty will grant him abundance throughout the entire year."""
"632","""Whoever spent one night of Rajab awake (in worship) and fasted for one day, Allah Almighty will feed him the fruits of Paradise."""
"633","""Whoever fasts three days in Rajab, Allah Almighty records for him the reward of fasting for a whole month."""
"634","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked, 'Which fasts are the most virtuous after Ramadan?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, 'Those of the month of Sha'ban.'"""
"635","""The first day of fasting among the White Days (i.e., the 13th, 14th, and 15th of the lunar month) is equal to three thousand years, the second day is equal to ten thousand years, and the third day is equal to thirteen thousand years."""
"636","“If someone observes a voluntary fast, even if he is given gold equal to the earth in return, its reward is still not fully given.”"
"637","""Whoever observed a voluntary fast and no one came to know about it, Allah Almighty will please him in return by granting him nothing less than Paradise."""
"638","""The fasting person is (at every moment) in worship, even if he is sleeping on his bed."""
"639","""Hajj and Umrah are both obligatory."""
"640","""If you perform Umrah, it is better for you."""
"641","""Hajj, Jihad, and Umrah are voluntary acts."""
"642","""Whoever has the means for the journey to the House of Allah, including travel expenses and conveyance, and yet does not perform Hajj, then it does not matter if he dies as a Jew or a Christian."""
"643","""Whoever got married before performing Hajj has begun sin and disobedience."""
"644","""When a pilgrim leaves his home, he is under Allah's protection. If he dies before completing the rites of Hajj, Allah forgives his previous sins."""
"645","""If people knew what virtue the pilgrims have over them, they would come to them even to the extent of washing their feet."""
"646","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed ‘Aqiq as the miqat for the people of the East."""
"647","""Whoever dons the Ihram for Hajj or Umrah from Masjid Al-Aqsa and proceeds towards Masjid Al-Haram, all his past and future sins will be forgiven, or Paradise will become obligatory for him."""
"648","""When Hazrat Ka'b bin Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) had pain in his head, he shaved his head. Upon this, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered him to sacrifice a cow."""
"649","""We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and women and children were with us. So we recited the Talbiyah on behalf of the children and also performed the Rami for them."""
"650","""When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished reciting the Talbiyah, he would ask Allah for His pleasure and for Paradise, and seek refuge from the Fire of Hell through Allah's mercy."""
"651","""When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would see the House of Allah, he would raise both his hands and make this supplication «اللهم زد هذا البيت تشريفا و تعظيما وتكريما ومهابة ، وزد من شرفه وكرمه ممن حجه واعتمره تشريفا وتعظيما وتكريما وبرا» ."""
"652","""The House of Allah has a Lord who protects it."""
"653","""Allah Almighty has promised regarding this House (i.e., the Ka'bah) that every year (at least) six hundred thousand people will perform Hajj to it."""
"654","""Allah Almighty said: When I intend to destroy the world, I will first destroy My House, and then after that, I will destroy the world."""
"655","“Seventy thousand angels have been appointed at the Rukn Yamani, so whoever says (Arabic text), all the angels will say Ameen. And whoever performs Tawaf of the Ka'bah and only says these words (Arabic text), ten of his sins will be erased, ten good deeds will be written for him, and his rank will be elevated by ten degrees.”"
"656","""Whoever performs Tawaf for a week in the rain, his past sins will be forgiven."""
"657","""Whoever performs ablution excellently and walks between Safa and Marwah, Allah Almighty writes seventy thousand ranks for him in exchange for every step."""
"658","""The water of Zamzam and the fire of Hell can never be combined in the belly of any servant."""
"659","""Indeed, for the mounted pilgrim, there are 70 good deeds for every step taken by his mount, and for the one who walks, there are 700 good deeds for every step."""
"660","""In the completion of Hajj, the slaughtering of camels is also included."""
"661","""In the completion of Hajj, it is also included that you assume Ihram from the area of your family and dependents."""
"662","""Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of my Ummah is like the mother of Musa (peace be upon him), who used to breastfeed him and also receive compensation for it from Pharaoh."""
"663","""Whoever dies on the way to Makkah while performing Hajj, Allah Almighty will neither confront him nor take his account."""
"664","""Whoever dies in either of the two Harams, my intercession becomes obligatory for him."""
"665","""Whoever called Madinah 'Yathrib' should seek forgiveness from Allah three times."""
"666","""Whoever performs forty prayers consecutively in my mosque, without missing any prayer, will have written for him freedom from the Fire, salvation from punishment, and freedom from hypocrisy."""
"667","""Whoever visits me in Medina with the intention of reward, I will be a witness and intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"668","""Whoever intentionally visits me will be under my protection on the Day of Judgment."""
"669","""Whoever visits me and my father Ibrahim (peace be upon him) in the same year will enter Paradise."""
"670","""Whoever performed the (prescribed) Hajj of Islam, visited my grave, participated in a battle, and sent blessings upon me after reaching Bayt al-Maqdis, then Allah Almighty will not question him about the obligations."""
"671","""Whoever has the means and does not come to me (that is, to visit my grave), then he has wronged me."""
"672","""Whoever performed Hajj on behalf of his parents or paid off their debt, Allah Almighty will raise him on the Day of Resurrection among the righteous."""
"673","“Diseases are gifts from Allah for a servant, so among the servants, the most beloved to Allah is the one who receives the most gifts.”"
"674","“ Illness descends all at once, but health descends little by little. ”"
"675","“Calamity and hardship will make the face of the afflicted white on the day when faces will be blackened.”"
"676","“If in this world Allah takes away someone’s eyesight, then it is a right upon Allah that his eyes will not see the fire of Hell.”"
"677","""When a person remains ill for three days, he becomes free from sins as if on that day his mother had given birth to him."""
"678","""Do not pretend to be ill, you will become ill; and do not dig your graves, you will die."""
"679","""The prayers of five people are accepted: the prayer of the oppressed until he takes revenge; the prayer of the pilgrim until he returns (home); the prayer of the warrior until he sits among his family; the prayer of the sick until he recovers; and the prayer of a brother for his brother in his absence. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Of all these prayers, the one that is accepted the quickest is the prayer of a brother for his brother in his absence."""
"680","""Visit the sick and ask them to pray for you, for the prayer of the sick is accepted and their sins are forgiven."""
"681","""When any of you has a sick person who desires some food, then let him feed him."""
"682","""Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then visits his Muslim brother with the intention of reward, he will be kept away from Hell by a distance of seventy (70) years."""
"683","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit the sick (for inquiry) three days after the onset of illness."""
"684","""Whoever visits a sick person and sits with him for a while, Allah Almighty grants him the reward of a thousand years."""
"685","""In my view, visiting a sick person is more beloved than forty or fifty years of worship."""
"686","""Do not neglect visiting the sick."""
"687","""Do not visit three types of patients: one with an eye ailment, one with a toothache, and one with a boil."""
"688","""Do not visit the one who does not visit you when you are ill."""
"689","""When you visit a sick person, give him reassurance about his death, for indeed this reassurance does not avert anything, but it pleases the soul of the patient."""
"690","""Whoever dies in a state of illness has died the death of a martyr."""
"691","""The death of a traveler is martyrdom."""
"692","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to seek refuge from seven types of death: sudden death, snake bite, being attacked by a wild animal, drowning, burning, falling upon something or something falling upon you, and being killed while fleeing during battle."""
"693","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to seek refuge from sudden death and preferred to be ill before death."""
"694","""Death alone is sufficient as a preacher."""
"695","""The deprived one is he who remained deprived of the essence."""
"696","""Instruct your dying ones to say these words, (Arabic text)"""
"697","""Whoever dies in Bayt al-Maqdis, it is as if he died in the heavens."""
"698","""If a single drop of the agony of death were placed upon all the mountains of the earth, they would melt."""
"699","""When the soul of a believer departs, the angels of mercy take it and say, 'Let him rest, for he endured many hardships in the world.'"""
"700","""Death is an expiation for every Muslim."""
"701","""Death is an expiation for the believer."""
"702","""Recite Surah Yaseen near your deceased ones."""
"703","""Upon the deceased over whom Surah Yaseen is recited, Allah Almighty grants ease to him."""
"704","""Your deeds are presented to your deceased close relatives; if the deeds are good, they become happy, and if they are not good, they pray: O Allah! Do not cause them to die until You guide them as You have guided us."""
"705","""Do not disgrace your deceased because of your bad deeds, for your deeds are presented to your friends who are in the graves."""
"706","""Whoever recites «انا لله وانا اليه راجعون» at the time of calamity, Allah Almighty compensates his loss, grants him a good outcome, and gives him in return something that he likes."""
"707","""My Ummah has been given, at the time of calamity (to say), something which no (other) Ummah has been given (and that is) «إنا لله وإنا اليه راجعون» ."" """
"708","""Because of the weeping of the living, hot water is sprinkled on the deceased."""
"709","""(O Ali!) Do not delay in three matters (one of them is) when a funeral is present (then in taking it for burial)."""
"710","""It is not permissible to keep the dead body of a Muslim among his family members."""
"711","""Treat your men as you treat brides."""
"712","""The one who bathes the deceased becomes free from sins as if the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"713","""If a woman passes away among men and there is no other woman present, or if a man passes away among women and there is no other man present, then they should be given tayammum and buried, and both will be like the person who does not have water."""
"714","“Hazrat Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) bathed herself and put on the shroud before her death. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was content with this.”"
"715","""Give a bath to your slain ones (martyrs)."""
"716","""Do not expose your thigh, and do not look at anyone's thigh, whether he is alive or dead."""
"717","""Do not give very expensive shrouds because they become worn out very quickly."""
"718","""Give your dead good shrouds because they visit each other in the graves."""
"719","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was shrouded in seven garments."""
"720","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a funeral, and the people were carrying it quickly, so he (peace be upon him) said: 'You should be calm and composed.'"""
"721","""(The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked about walking with the funeral procession, so he, peace and blessings be upon him, replied:) A pace that is less than running."""
"722","""Whoever attends a funeral should shoulder the (deceased's) bier from all four sides."""
"723","""Whoever carries the bier from all four sides, Allah Almighty forgives forty major sins of his."""
"724","""Give your dying ones the provision of the Kalimah «لا اله الا الله» ."""
"725","""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was walking behind a funeral, only this phrase «لا اله الا الله» was heard from him."""
"726","""After the death of a (believing) servant, the very first reward given to him is that all those who walk behind his funeral are forgiven."""
"727","""The honor of a believer with Allah is that He forgives those who walk with his funeral."""
"728","""Do you not feel ashamed that Allah's angels are walking on their feet while you are riding?"""
"729","“Do not walk ahead of the funeral (procession).”"
"730","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to walk behind the funeral procession."""
"731","""(The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was attending a funeral when Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was startled upon seeing a woman. So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) O Umar! Leave her alone."""
"732","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once came out of his house and saw some women sitting on the way. He asked: Why are you sitting here? They replied: We are waiting for a funeral. Upon hearing this, he rebuked them and ordered them to return."""
"733","“There is no good in women’s congregation except in the mosque or for the funeral of a murdered person.”"
"734","""There is no reward for women in following the funeral procession."""
"735","""Whoever, upon seeing a funeral, says: «الله اكبر صدق الله ورسوله هذا ما وعدنا الله ورسوله اللهم زدنا ايمانا وتسليما» , twenty good deeds are written for him every day from that day until the Day of Resurrection."""
"736","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not make anything as permissible for us as they made permissible in the funeral prayer for the deceased, that is, they did not fix a specific time for it."""
"737","""Offer the funeral prayer for your children."""
"738","“The funeral prayer of the child will not be offered.”"
"739","""When a premature child cries out, his funeral prayer will be offered and he will also be made an heir."""
"740","""The last (funeral prayer) takbirs that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said were four."""
"741","""The angels offered the funeral prayer of Hazrat Adam (peace be upon him) and said four takbirs."""
"742","""We have been commanded to recite Surah Al-Fatihah over our deceased."""
"743","""Whoever offered the funeral prayer in the mosque, there is nothing (reward) for him."""
"744","""The one who dies by drowning should be left for one day and night, then buried."""
"745","""Bury your dead among righteous people, for the deceased also feels distress from a bad neighbor just as a living person feels distress from a bad neighbor."""
"746","""Every house has a door, and the door of the grave is at its feet."""
"747","""A woman has two veils: the grave and her husband."""
"748","“The punishment of the grave is true, and whoever does not believe in it will be punished in it.”"
"749","“Water was sprinkled on the grave of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) sprinkled water from a waterskin on the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He began sprinkling from the head side and continued sprinkling water up to the foot side.”"
"750","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sprinkled water on the grave of his son Ibrahim and placed pebbles on it."""
"751","""The prolonged stay of my Ummah in the graves is a means for the cleansing of their sins."""
"752","""Whoever comforts a person afflicted by a calamity will have a reward similar to that of the afflicted one."""
"753","""Do not express joy over your brother's misfortune; Allah, the Exalted, will have mercy on him and will put you to trial."""
"754","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed women who visit graves."""
"755","""Whoever visits his mother's grave, it is as if he has performed Umrah."""
"756","""Whoever greets the dead, they will respond to him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"757","""The sin of breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking the bone of a living person."""
"758","""(When Abu Razin asked, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, taught him this supplication to recite when passing by the graves of the people «السلام عليكم يا اهل القبور» : Peace be upon you, O inhabitants of the graves! So he said: O Messenger of Allah! Do they hear? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: They hear, but they do not have the power to respond.)"""
"759","""Indeed, Allah Almighty sends down mercies upon the inhabitants of the graves, as great as mountains, because of the supplication of the people of the earth."""
"760","""Whoever refrained from marriage out of fear of poverty is not from among us."""
"761","""Whoever has the ability to marry and does not marry, he has no relation with me."""
"762","""The best helper and supporter in matters of religion is a righteous wife."""
"763","""After the fear of Allah, the best benefit for a believing man is a righteous wife."""
"764","""Shall I not inform you about the best treasure of a man? (And that is) a righteous wife."""
"765","""Your unmarried people are the worst."""
"766","“If even one day of my life remains, I will still meet my wife for the sake of Allah Almighty (Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him).”"
"767","""Two rak'ahs of a married person are superior to seventy rak'ahs of an unmarried person."""
"768","""The unmarried is a warrant for the fire of Hell."""
"769","""A Bedouin complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about lust and hunger, so he (peace be upon him) instructed him: 'Marry the first woman you find who does not have a husband.'"""
"770","""When any of you wishes to marry a woman, just as he inquires about her face, he should also inquire about her hair, for hair too is a place of beauty."""
"771","""The Arabs are suitable matches for one another."""
"772","""Whoever wishes to meet Allah in a state of purity should marry free women."""
"773","""Free women are a means of the household’s rectification, and slave girls are a means of the household’s ruin."""
"774","""Whoever marries his daughter to a sinner (evildoer, disobedient person), surely he has severed ties with her."""
"775","“Do not marry women solely on the basis of kinship, for this very thing (later) becomes a cause of severing relations.”"
"776","""Whoever marries a woman for her honor, Allah increases him only in humiliation; whoever marries her for her wealth, Allah increases him only in poverty; whoever marries her for her beauty, Allah increases him only in baseness; and whoever marries for the sake of lowering his gaze, protecting his private parts, or joining ties of kinship, Allah places blessings for him in the woman and for the woman in him."""
"777","“Do not marry women for their beauty, for it is possible that their beauty may lead them to ruin, and do not marry them for their wealth, for it is possible that their wealth may make them rebellious. Rather, marry them on the basis of religion, and indeed a religious black slave woman with a pierced nose and cut nose is better than a beautiful and wealthy woman who lacks religion.”"
"778","“Do not marry a foolish woman, for her company is a trial and there is harm in her offspring.”"
"779","""Choose (women) thoughtfully for your offspring, because women give birth to children who resemble their brothers and sisters."""
"780","""Consult women regarding their daughters (because they know best the mental and moral state of their daughters, therefore they can tell whether you will be able to get along with them or not)."""
"781","""Umm Salamah and Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with them) were with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when suddenly Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him. Upon this, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Both of you observe veiling from him.' Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: 'O Messenger of Allah! This person is blind; he cannot see us.' So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Are you both blind as well? Do you not see him?'"""
"782","""The first love of Islam is the love of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) for Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."""
"783","""The dower (mahr) is not less than ten dirhams."""
"784","""The best woman among you is the one whose dowry is easy (that is, because her dowry is less, its payment is easy)."""
"785","""The most blessed woman is the one whose expenses (i.e., dowry and the like) are the least."""
"786","""Announce the marriage, hold it in the mosques, and beat the duff in it."""
"787","""When the Prophet (peace be upon him) married a woman, the people scattered Ajwa dates over his head."""
"788","""Deceit, trickery, and fraud are only permissible in marriage."""
"789","""Those women are adulteresses who marry themselves off without witnesses."""
"790","""Whoever marries a woman should give her a gift before going near her, even if it is only one of his shoes."""
"791","""When any of you has intercourse, he should not look towards the private parts, because this leads to blindness."""
"792","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""I never saw the private parts of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"793","""Whoever looks at the private part of a woman, then her mother and daughter do not remain lawful for him (i.e., now he cannot marry either of them)."""
"794","""None of you should speak excessively during intercourse, because this may cause the child to be born mute."""
"795","""It is obligatory for a man to adorn himself for his wife in the same way as it is obligatory for a woman for him."""
"796","""I have only forbidden you from looting the spoils of war, not from partaking in wedding feasts."""
"797","""Women's desire is twice that of men."""
"798","“It is not permissible for any woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to expose any part of her hair or chest before a Jew, Christian, or Magian, and whoever does so has no trustworthiness.”"
"799","""A woman who leaves her husband's house without his permission, everything upon which the sun and the moon rise curses her, unless her husband becomes pleased with her."""
"800","""A woman should not leave her house without her husband's permission; if she does so, the angels of the sky, the angels of mercy, and the angels of punishment (all) will curse her until she returns."""
"801","""Obedience to women leads to regret."""
"802","""Whoever is patient with his wife's bad character, Allah Almighty will grant him a reward equal to the reward given to Ayub (peace be upon him) for his trial. And whichever woman is patient with her husband's bad character, Allah Almighty will grant her a reward equal to the reward given to Asiya (peace be upon her), the wife of Pharaoh."""
"803","""Do not let them (women) reside in upper chambers, nor teach them writing and literacy; teach them spinning yarn and teach them Surah An-Nur."""
"804","""Only an honorable person shows respect to women, and only a vile person humiliates them."""
"805","""The wife's slave has perished."""
"806","""Consult with them (women) but oppose them."""
"807","""None of you should do any work until he consults, and if there is no one to consult, then consult a woman, then oppose her advice, because there is blessing in opposing her."""
"808","""Remove the women's clothes (so that) they remain seated in their designated place of seclusion within the house."""
"809","""The example of a righteous wife among women is like that of one crow among a hundred crows."""
"810","""A woman's jihad is to obey her husband (and to treat him with good conduct)."""
"811","“If a woman dies while her husband is pleased with her, she will enter Paradise.”"
"812","""The pious widow has been given the title of martyr (shaheeda) in the heavens."""
"813","""I do not like men who are tasters nor women who are tasters. (Imam Ibn Athir, may Allah have mercy on him, explained its meaning as those who are hasty in marriage and also hasty in divorce.) [النهايته] """
"814","""Whoever goes to arrange the marriage of two people, Allah Almighty will grant him the reward of one year for every step and every word, and whoever goes to separate two people, it is incumbent upon Allah Almighty to strike his head on a thousand rocks in Hell on the Day of Judgment."""
"815","""O Mu'adh! Allah Almighty has not created anything on the surface of the earth that is more beloved to Him than freeing (slaves), and Allah Almighty has not created anything on the surface of the earth that is more disliked to Him than divorce."""
"816","""The slave woman has two divorces and her waiting period is two menstruations."""
"817","“How should the right of suckling (the one who breastfeeds) be fulfilled?” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “By giving a slave man or a slave woman as payment.”"
"818","""Do not let a foolish woman breastfeed your children."""
"819","""There is no li'an between four types of people: between a free man and a slave woman, between a free woman and a slave man, between a Muslim man and a Jewish woman, and between a Muslim man and a Christian woman."""
"820","“Marry and have children, for on the Day of Judgment I wish to boast of your (great numbers) before the other nations.”"
"821","""A son is the secret of his father."""
"822","""On the day Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) was born, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the adhan in his right ear and the iqamah in his left ear."""
"823","""Whoever names (his child) after my name should not take my kunya, and whoever takes my kunya should not name (his child) after my name."""
"824","""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection you will be called by your names and the names of your fathers, so keep good names for yourselves."""
"825","“Circumcision is Sunnah for men and a matter of honor for women.”"
"826","“A man who is uncircumcised will not be tolerated in Islam until he gets circumcised, even if he is eighty years old.”"
"827","""A man who is uncircumcised cannot perform Hajj of the House of Allah until he gets circumcised."""
"828","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was born circumcised."""
"829","""Whoever is a Muslim should perform circumcision, even if he is of advanced age."""
"830","""Teach your sons swimming and archery."""
"831","""It is better for a man to teach good manners to his children than to give a sa’ (approximately two and a half kilograms of grain) in charity."""
"832","""A father has not given his child any gift better than good manners."""
"833","""The child has a right over the father that he gives him a good name and teaches him good manners."""
"834","""Do not beat your children for crying."""
"835","""Whoever placed his hand with mercy and compassion on the head of an orphan, for every hair over which his hand passed, there is a good deed for him as a reward."""
"836","""A man complained about having few children, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) instructed him to eat eggs and onions."""
"837","""Love daughters, for I too am a father of daughters."""
"838","""Whoever spends a dirham on the marriage of his son or daughter, Allah Almighty will grant him twelve cities in Paradise for every dirham spent."""
"839","""The drop of fluid from which a child is created causes all the limbs and veins to tremble."""
"840","""The small number of family members is an ease; their abundance is a poverty."""
"841","""Give your children a kunyah before nicknames become prevalent over them."""
"842","""Whoever raised a child until he began to say the Kalimah 'La ilaha illallah', Allah the Exalted will not take account from him."""
"843","""May Allah have mercy on the father who assists his child in doing good deeds."""
"844","""Be equal among your children when giving gifts."""
"845","""The prayer of a father for his child is like the prayer of a prophet for his community."""
"846","""Be good to your parents and your sons will be good to you."""
"847","""Kindness to parents is superior to prayer, fasting, Hajj, Umrah, and striving in the way of Allah."""
"848","""The fragrance of Paradise will be sensed from a distance of five hundred years, but the one who is disobedient to his parents will be deprived of its fragrance."""
"849","""When a person stops praying for their parents, sustenance from their children in this world is cut off."""
"850","""If I find my parents or even one of them, and I am offering the Isha prayer, having already recited Surah Al-Fatihah in it, and they call me, 'O Muhammad!' then I will respond to them, saying, 'Here I am.'"""
"851","""Whoever kissed between his mother's eyes, this act will become a barrier for him from the fire of Hell."""
"852","""The time of death came for a young man; due to his disobedience to his mother, he was unable to recite the Kalimah. Then the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) interceded with his mother, and when she became pleased, he was then able to recite the Kalimah."""
"853","""The one who is obedient to parents and the Lord will be in the highest ranks of ‘Illiyyin."""
"854","""If a person's parents or one of them passes away and he was disobedient to them, but then he continues to pray and seek forgiveness for them, he is recorded by Allah as one who is dutiful and obedient."""
"855","""Whoever looks at his parents with a gaze of mercy, Allah Almighty writes for him the reward of an accepted Hajj for every such gaze. The companions asked, 'Even if he looks a hundred (100) times a day?' The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, 'Yes, Allah Almighty is the Greatest and Most Pure.'"""
"856","""They are your Paradise (if you obey them) and your Hell (if you disobey them)."""
"857","""Whenever the lawful and the unlawful are combined, the unlawful prevails."""
"858","""Whoever eats a morsel of the forbidden, his prayer is not accepted for forty days."""
"859","""Whoever abandons a single dirham of the unlawful, Allah, the Lord of Majesty, will free him from the fire of Hell."""
"860","""Whoever is not upright in matters of livelihood is not upright in matters of religion either."""
"861","""Allah Almighty dislikes an idle youth."""
"862","""Allah Almighty dislikes an idle person."""
"863","""If my servant feels shy of the lawful, Allah Almighty afflicts him with the unlawful."""
"864","""Whoever acquires wealth through unlawful means, Allah Almighty leads him into destruction."""
"865","""An angel of Allah Almighty is present at Bayt al-Maqdis, who announces every night that whoever has consumed the unlawful, neither any of his voluntary worship will be accepted nor any obligatory."""
"866","""If the people of Paradise were to engage in trade, they would trade in cloth."""
"867","“A cowardly trader is deprived, and a brave trader is given sustenance.”"
"868","""Learn calligraphy, for indeed it is the key to sustenance."""
"869","""The worst people are traders and farmers."""
"870","""The worst wealth in the end times will be slaves and slave-girls."""
"871","""The miserly people of my Ummah are tailors."""
"872","""O Allah! Do not let us accept the opinion of the trader and the traveler among us, because our trader desires high prices and our traveler dislikes rain."""
"873","""Whoever wished for inflation upon my Ummah even for one night, Allah Almighty will destroy his forty years of deeds."""
"874","""The one who brings goods to the market is provided with sustenance, and a curse is invoked upon the one who hoards."""
"875","""Whoever hoards grain for forty days will be disassociated from Allah, and Allah will be disassociated from him."""
"876","""Whoever hoards grain from the Muslims for forty days, then even if he gives all of it in charity, it will not be an expiation for him."""
"877","""Every loan that brings benefit is usury."""
"878","""Modesty withholds sustenance."""
"879","""Washing utensils and cleaning the courtyard (both actions) make one prosperous."""
"880","""When you have performed the Fajr prayer, do not sleep (out of heedlessness) instead of seeking sustenance."""
"881","""There are two types which Allah Almighty has honored in this world and the Hereafter: one is gold and the other is silver. Allah Almighty has made them a source of dignity for the people of this world and a source of adornment for the people of the Hereafter."""
"882","""The dirham is so named because it is the abode of grief, and the dinar is so named because it is the abode of fire."""
"883","""Allah Almighty created sustenance two thousand years before the creation of bodies."""
"884","""Do not buy fish in water because this is deception."""
"885","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of a deferred item for another deferred item."""
"886","""Whoever bought something without seeing it, then after seeing it, he has the choice (if he likes it, he may keep it, otherwise he may return it)."""
"887","""There is no right of pre-emption for the absent or for a child, and pre-emption is like untying a rope."""
"888","""Allah Almighty says that I am the third among two partners as long as one of them does not betray his companion."""
"889","""The pawned item will not be withheld from its owner; its benefit is also for him, and he is also responsible for its liability."""
"890","""Washing hands before eating is one virtue, while washing hands after eating is the cause of two virtues."""
"891","""Washing hands before eating removes poverty and hunger."""
"892","""Washing hands before and after eating is a means of abundance in sustenance and of removing satanic ways."""
"893","""The blessing of food is in performing ablution before and after it."""
"894","""Whoever forgets to say Bismillah before eating should recite Surah Al-Ikhlas (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad) after finishing."""
"895","""O Ali! Be sure to use salt, for it is a cure for seventy diseases, such as leprosy, vitiligo, and madness (etc.)."""
"896","""Whoever begins his morning meal with salt, Allah Almighty will remove seventy kinds of diseases from him."""
"897","""The leader of your condiments is salt."""
"898","""Whoever picks up and eats the morsel that falls from the dining cloth or utensil (after cleaning it), he is saved from poverty, foolishness, and the disease of leprosy."""
"899","""Whoever eats from a vessel and then licks it, the vessel seeks forgiveness for him."""
"900","""When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished eating, he would recite this supplication «الحمد لله الذى أطعمنا وسقانا وجعلنا مسلمين» ."""
"901","""When you eat or drink something and recite this supplication «بسم الله الذى لا يضر مع اسمه شىء فى الارض ولا فى السماء يا حى يا قيوم» , then no illness will befall you from that food, even if it contains poison."""
"902","""Food in the market is inferiority."""
"903","""Respect bread, for Allah Almighty has sent down the blessings of the sky for it and has brought forth the blessings of the earth for it."""
"904","""Respect bread because Allah Almighty also respects it, and whoever respects bread, Allah Almighty will also respect him."""
"905","""Any nation that considers the right of bread to be insignificant, Allah Almighty afflicts it with hunger."""
"906","""Do not cut bread with a knife as the non-Arabs do."""
"907","""Keep the bread small and increase its number; there will be blessing placed in it for you."""
"908","“O Allah! Benefit us through Islam and bread; if there were no bread, we would neither fast, nor pray, nor perform Hajj, nor engage in Jihad.”"
"909","""Three meals will not be accounted for a person: the pre-dawn meal (suhoor), the meal with which one breaks the fast (iftar), and the meal eaten together with brothers."""
"910","""Blowing on food takes away the blessing."""
"911","""Those who spend the night with a full stomach have good manners, and those who spend the night hungry have bad manners."""
"912","""If the Prophet (peace be upon him) ate in the morning, he would not eat in the evening, and if he ate in the evening, he would not eat in the morning."""
"913","""Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ate food, he would praise Allah and then recite this supplication «اللهم بارك لنا فيه و أطعمنا أطيب منه» ."""
"914","""The chief of the food of the people of the world and the people of Paradise is meat."""
"915","""Indeed, the heart feels joy and happiness when eating meat."""
"916","""Meat produces (nourishes) flesh, and whoever abstains from meat for forty days, his creation (appearance and form) becomes bad."""
"917","""Eat olives and apply its oil, for it is pure and blessed."""
"918","""Drinking milk is pure faith; whoever drinks milk in a dream is upon faith and natural disposition."""
"919","""It is a sign of humility that a person drinks the leftover water of his brother, and whoever drinks his brother's leftover water for the sake of Allah's pleasure, seventy ranks are elevated for him."""
"920","""Whoever gives a Muslim a sip of water where water is available, it is as if he has freed a slave; and whoever gives a Muslim a sip of water where water is not available, it is as if he has given life to a believing soul."""
"921","""Give water to drink upon water during hot days; your sins will fall away just as leaves fall from a tree in a strong, fierce wind."""
"922","""In food, rice is like a leader among a people."""
"923","""Whoever eats rice for forty days, springs of wisdom flow from his heart to his tongue."""
"924","""Rice is from me and I am from rice. I created rice from the remainder of my light."""
"925","""Certainly use lentils because they are blessed and pure."""
"926","""Certainly use lentils, for they were sanctified on the tongues of seventy prophets."""
"927","""There is a cure for every disease in eggplant, and there is no disease in it."""
"928","""Eat eggplant in abundance, for indeed it is the first tree that I saw in Paradise al-Ma'wa."""
"929","""Melon, before eating food, washes the stomach and completely eliminates illness."""
"930","""The springtime of my Ummah is grapes and melon."""
"931","""Eat bottle gourd, for it increases intelligence."""
"932","""O Ali! When you take provisions for the journey, do not forget onions."""
"933","""Certainly use onions, because they purify the sperm and a child is born."""
"934","""Whoever ate cucumber with meat was protected from the disease of leprosy."""
"935","""The heart of a believer is sweet; it likes only sweetness."""
"936","""Indeed, those who are hungry in this world will be satisfied in the Hereafter."""
"937","""Cheese is a disease and walnut is also a disease, but when the two are combined, they become a cure."""
"938","""The chief of oils is violet oil, and the superiority of violet oil among oils is like the superiority of Islam among all religions."""
"939","“There will be blessings in the house of the one who has a goat in his house.”"
"940","""Do not abuse the rooster because it is my friend and I am its friend."""
"941","""(Abu al-Bakhtari went to Caliph Harun al-Rashid and found him flying pigeons. Seeing this, he fabricated and narrated this tradition to please the Caliph:) The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to fly pigeons."""
"942","""Except for the crow and the vulture, there is no harm in eating all birds."""
"943","""The porcupine... is one of the impure animals among the impure animals."""
"944","""Indeed, this is extravagance: eat whenever you wish."""
"945",""" Eating soil leads to hypocrisy. """
"946",""" Eating soil is forbidden for every Muslim."""
"947","""Whoever ate soil and bathed with it, (it is as if) he has eaten the flesh of his father Adam (peace be upon him) and bathed with his blood."""
"948","The companions asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What are these sacrifices?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""It is the tradition of your father Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."" The companions asked, ""What reward is there for us in them?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""For every hair, there is a good deed."""
"949","A man asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) about sacrifice, whether it is obligatory. He replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the Muslims have performed sacrifice. Then he asked you the same question again, so you said: Do you understand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the Muslims have performed sacrifice."
"950","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) resided in Madinah for ten years and offered sacrifice (Qurbani) every year."""
"951","""On the tenth of Dhul-Hijjah, the son of Adam does not perform any deed more beloved to Allah than shedding blood (offering sacrifice). These animals will come on the Day of Resurrection with their horns, hooves, and hair. Before the blood falls to the ground, it attains a position with Allah. So, offer your sacrifice with a cheerful heart."""
"952","""(Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said that) the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, advised me to offer a sacrifice on his behalf, so I offer a sacrifice on his behalf."""
"953","“Agarwood, sandalwood, musk, amber, and camphor are the garments of Adam (peace be upon him) in which he was sent down from Paradise.”"
"954","""The man's knee is included in the 'awrah (private parts to be covered)."""
"955","""Offering prayer with a turban is equal to twenty-five prayers (without a turban), and offering Friday prayer with a turban is equal to seventy Fridays (without a turban)."""
"956","""The reward for praying with a turban on the head is equal to that of jihad in the way of Allah."""
"957","""Tie the turban, you will increase in forbearance and patience."""
"958","""Certainly wear turbans, for indeed they are a sign of the angels."""
"959","""The distinction between us and the polytheists is tying turbans over caps."""
"960","""The angels' clothing reaches up to half of the shin."""
"961","""Fold your clothes (i.e., arrange them properly), their souls return to them. Indeed, if Satan finds folded clothes, he does not wear them, but if he finds scattered clothes, he wears them."""
"962","""Whoever wishes to sit with Allah should sit with those who wear woolen garments."""
"963","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away wearing woolen clothing."""
"964","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wear a waist-wrapper (belt) on his back."""
"965","""Whoever ties a camel and wears woolen clothing is free from arrogance."""
"966","""Whoever wears yellow shoes will remain in happiness as long as he keeps wearing them."""
"967","""The sign of a hypocrite is that his trousers are long."""
"968","""Prayer with a ring is equal to seventy prayers without a ring."""
"969","""Wear a ring of aqeeq, it is blessed."""
"970","""Most of the gems in Paradise are of agate."""
"971","""Whoever wears an aqeeq ring will always see goodness and virtue."""
"972","""Whoever wears a ring with a ruby stone, Allah Almighty removes his poverty."""
"973","""Wear emerald (a precious stone); it is easy, there is nothing difficult in it."""
"974","""Spending in the way of Allah is equal to seven hundred dirhams, whereas spending one dirham for applying dye is equal to seven thousand dirhams."""
"975","""The one who dies with dye applied (to the hair), Munkar and Nakir will not question him in the grave."""
"976","""Whoever kept long mustaches in the world, Allah, the Lord of Honor, will lengthen his regret on the Day of Resurrection."""
"977","""The angels of the sky seek forgiveness for women with locks on their foreheads and men with beards, and they say: 'Glory be to the One who adorned men with beards and women with locks.'"""
"978","""None of you should cut the beard, however, he may trim the hair of the temples."""
"979","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to trim his beard from the length and the width."""
"980","""Whoever combs his head and beard every night is granted protection from various kinds of trials, and his lifespan is also increased."""
"981","""Whoever combs his hair while standing, debt mounts upon him."""
"982","""The comb never parted from the Prophet (peace be upon him) during travel or at home."""
"983","""Whoever cuts their nails on Saturday, illness departs from them and healing enters into them."""
"984","""Indeed, the rose flower was created from the sweat of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"985","""On the night I was taken on the journey (that is, the night of Mi'raj), some of my sweat fell upon the earth, and from it the rose flower grew. So whoever wishes to smell my fragrance should smell the rose."""
"986","""When fragrance is brought to any one of you, he should certainly apply it, and when something sweet is brought, he should also certainly eat it."""
"987","""The chief of the fragrant plants of Paradise is henna."""
"988","""Frankincense (the gum of a thorny tree) is the fragrance of mine and the angels."""
"989","""Smell the narcissus flower, whether once a day, once a month, once a year, or even once in a lifetime."""
"990","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) would apply kohl every night, undergo cupping every month, and take medicine every year."""
"991","""In cases of insanity, leprosy, and vitiligo, cupping should be done on the head."""
"992","""Whoever wants to get cupping done should do so on the seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first (of the lunar month)."""
"993","“Get cupped on the fifteenth, seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first of the (lunar) month.”"
"994","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade cupping on Saturday and Wednesday."""
"995","""On Friday, there is an hour in which if a person undergoes cupping, he will die."""
"996","""One day of fever is an expiation for the sins of a year."""
"997","“There is a cure for every illness in drinking the leftover water from a believer’s ablution, the least of which is sorrow.”"
"998","""The saliva of a believer is also a cure."""
"999","""The food of a miser is disease, whereas the food of a generous person is cure."""
"1000","""The stomach is the home of diseases, and abstinence is the foundation of medicine."""
"1001","""The stomach is the reservoir of the body; all the veins descend into it. If the stomach is healthy, the veins will return with health, and if the stomach is corrupt, the veins will return with disease."""
"1002","""The remedy for the eye is that it should not be touched."""
"1003","""The loss of eyesight is forgiveness of sins, the loss of hearing is forgiveness of sins, and similarly, every harm to the body is a means of forgiveness of sins."""
"1004","""The affliction of one foot of a person becomes a means for the forgiveness of half of his sins, while the affliction of both feet becomes a means for the forgiveness of all his sins."""
"1005","""Whoever licks honey on an empty stomach three days every month will not be afflicted with any major illness."""
"1006","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) held the hand of a leprosy patient and placed it in the vessel that was present with him, and said: 'Join in eating, trusting and relying upon Allah Almighty.'"""
"1007","""In medicine, the last treatment is cauterization."""
"1008","""Surah Al-Fatihah is a cure for every illness."""
